      "sourceText": "# Source-grounded explanation\n\n## Development input\n\nOrigin: adapted event summaries from a public discussion\nSource: https://github.com/eslint/rfcs/pull/134\nCutoff: 2025-06-26T23:59:59Z\n\n- 2025-05-21T18:22:25Z · MorevM · opening · 3081073479: The PR author proposes shareable per-rule autofix control, continuing an earlier RFC and inviting feedback on an incomplete draft and implementation plan.\n- 2025-05-21T18:22:32Z · linux-foundation-easycla[bot] · comment · 2898850775: An automated CLA check records signed agreement status for the listed contributors.\n- 2025-06-10T22:32:56Z · MorevM · comment · 2960728262: The author challenges a claimed performance cost of object-shaped rule entries and offers a small benchmark, while acknowledging its limited realism.\n- 2025-06-11T14:38:26Z · nzakas · comment · 2963101004: A maintainer says the concern is retaining both array and object forms in memory and prefers a nonbreaking helper syntax backed by a separate autofix map.\n- 2025-06-11T15:55:08Z · MorevM · comment · 2963362746: The author revisits memory measurements and argues the overhead may be acceptable, while questioning how a top-level setting would interact with rule entries.\n- 2025-06-13T14:35:39Z · nzakas · comment · 2970605137: The maintainer reiterates that simultaneous internal representations, rather than either representation alone, are the concern; defineConfig could translate user syntax.\n- 2025-06-13T15:35:29Z · MorevM · comment · 2970769803: The author accepts the helper translation idea but asks which setting should win if both per-rule and top-level autofix declarations are allowed.\n- 2025-06-17T14:54:01Z · nzakas · comment · 2980705905: The maintainer suggests withholding top-level autofix from defineConfig initially, leaving lower-level configuration available to direct users.\n- 2025-06-25T21:32:04Z · MorevM · comment · 3006206582: The author asks whether helper-only syntax would remove proposed CLI and inline forms